- id: FRM-P43
  name: "Non-flat API body: dot-notation for nested; member-driven forms for discriminated/union — never a flat catch-all"
  when: "SDK mutation body is nested OR is a discriminated/variant union"
  reason: |
    Nested body (e.g. revenueTax.type) → dot-notation field names so TanStack types resolve.
    Discriminated/variant union body (ShippingFee by mode; ConnectIntegration's per-platform credentials)
    → the discriminant is a SELECTOR and each variant is validated against its CONCRETE SDK member.
    NEVER flatten a union into an all-optional catch-all (`uiSchema` / `z.record(z.string(),z.string())`)
    that re-declares the union's members — that throws away the contract and hand-rolls shapes (incl. money).
    Two shapes:
      (a) union is a FIELD of the body → make the form field BE the SDK union via `.pick({ field: true })`;
          the discriminant drives conditional rendering and the value comes from the member (no hand-roll).
      (b) union IS the body → ONE small form component per variant (duplication is fine), typed via
          `Extract<Req,{discriminant}>`, gated/validated by the SDK union's `safeParse` at submit.
  rule: |
    // Nested body — dot-notation:
    <form.Field name="revenueTax.type">...</form.Field>

    // (a) union is a field — pick it from the SDK, render by the discriminant (ShippingFeeForm):
    const formSchema = updateFeesMutationRequestSchema.pick({ shippingFee: true })
    <form.Field name="shippingFee.mode">{/* discriminant selector */}</form.Field>
    {MODES_WITH_VALUE.includes(mode) && <form.Field name="shippingFee.value">{/* CurrencyInput, SDK-derived */}</form.Field>}

    // (b) union IS the body — a form per variant, typed via Extract, validated by the SDK union (CredentialForms):
    type ShopifyVariant = Extract<ConnectIntegrationMutationRequest, { platform: 'SHOPIFY'; connectionMode: 'CREDENTIALS' }>
    const defaultValues: DeepPartial<ShopifyVariant> = { platform: 'SHOPIFY', connectionMode: 'CREDENTIALS', credentials: { shopDomain: '', ... } }
    // submit + button gate use the SDK union (it narrows to the member):
    const r = connectIntegrationMutationRequestSchema.safeParse(value); if (!r.success) return
